    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d68">

                <pb facs="0251" n="125" xml:id="pg125"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51 W 89Czechoslovakia/90: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Einstein</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Prague</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-05-02T13:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 2, 1925—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 4:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>12. Your instruction number 252, April 4th. Presented note today.<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d68-f1"/> Dr. Beneš denies any intention of discriminating against
                    the United States by arranging payment of so-called Nansen relief bonds and
                    believes such impression is based on misunderstanding. Will write me in
                    explanation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Einstein</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
